style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The next release, kirkstone =
will be 4.0 (previously known as 3.5) and will be bitbake 2.0 =
based.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The first release candidate =
build for YP 4.0 (3.5) is in QA but has at least one issue which will =
mean we need a second release candidate build. We will build that after =
the final QA report is back.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.3.6, the final hardknott =
release will build after 4.0 rc2.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are several issues which =
have arisen in the last week which mean we will need a second release =
candidate build:<o:p></o:p></span></li><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Dcircle><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level2 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>edgerouter didn&#8217;t boot =
with rc1 due to a kernel patch issue<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level2 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>uninative didn&#8217;t work =
with libstdc++ from gcc 12 so we have an upgraded =
version<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level2 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>there were several CVE fixes =
that came in (libarchive, gzip, xz)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level2 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>a key intermittent autobuilder =
fix was identified<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul></ul><p =
style=3D'margin:0in;text-indent:.5in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Not all of these =
were release blockers but together they mean an rc2 is =
appropriate.</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>If anyone is aware of other =
issues in rc1 that need to be addressed in rc2, please let us know =
ASAP.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 4.1 planning document is =
available for review at: <a =
href=3D"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-g7DatSdmIETwD3xFSCxV7MbWVVkp=
QvQ788mIr1MPTI/edit?usp=3Dsharing"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-g7DatSdmIETw=
D3xFSCxV7MbWVVkpQvQ788mIr1MPTI/edit?usp=3Dsharing</span></a><o:p></o:p></=
span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>If people see intermittent =
issues in their own builds, particularly if they&#8217;re the same as =
intermittent issues seen on the autobuilder, please do comment in the =
bugs mentioning when they happen as the frequency information does help =
us prioritize fixing the most common issues.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent issues continue to =
be at high levels and help is very much welcome in trying to resolve =
them. You can see the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by =
searching for the &#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
